####### # Setup #######
Context('Numeric'); $rational = PopUp(['?','rational','irrational'], 1); $irrational = PopUp(['?','rational','irrational'], 2);
###### # Body ######
BEGIN_PGML Imagine making up a number with the following pattern. After the decimal point, write the natural numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, etc. The decimal digits will extend forever with this pattern: [`0.12345\ldots\text{.}`]
Is the number a rational number or an irrational number? [_]{$irrational}{5}
END_PGML
########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION The number is irrational. The decimal will never end and it will never repeat.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
############# # End Problem #############
